<title>TURKEY: Turk Eregli 9-mth profits fall 66 pct.</title>
<headline>Turk Eregli 9-mth profits fall 66 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-Sept 1996 provisional</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira)	  466.18  vs   1,355.19</p>
<p>    Net profit			 2,953.70  vs   8,586.49</p>
<p>    Net sales			 47,258.39  vs  26,390.66</p>
<p>    Operating profit		10,441.87  vs   9,492.39</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	     2,330.59  vs   4,264.32</p>
<p>    Interest paid		    7,133.45  vs   2,704.15</p>
<p>    Extraordinary expense	  2,265.92  vs   1,286.20</p>
<p>    Total debts		     79,521.62  vs  41,842.35</p>
<p>    Equity			    32,732.15  vs  24,175.22</p>
<p>    Capital			    6,336.00  vs   6,336.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Turkey's biggest flat steel producer Eregli Demir ve Celik Fabrikalari A.S. is slated for privatisation, with 51.66 percent of its capital held by the privatisation agency OIB.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 79.3 percent year-on-year consumer price inflation in September.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875</p>
</text>
